\lispPackageChapter{candlesticks}

The umbrella package, defined with \texttt{uiop:define-package} and
\texttt{:reexport}.  Every public symbol from the sub-packages ---
including the version helpers from \texttt{candlesticks/system} --- is
used and re-exported, so that \texttt{(use-package :candlesticks)} ---
or simply \texttt{(in-package :candlesticks)} --- gives you the whole
library at once.  New exports on a sub-package show up here without
editing this file.

\section{Functions}

\lispFunctionSubsection{version-string}

The library version as a dotted string, currently \texttt{"0.2.0"}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{version-list}

The library version as a list of three integers,
\texttt{(\lispVar{major} \lispVar{minor} \lispVar{revision})}.

The parameters \lispId{version-major}, \lispId{version-minor}, and
\lispId{version-revision} hold the three pieces separately.
